WEBVTT

00:00:05.885 --> 00:00:11.866
<v><b> Speaker:</b></v> The best or worst thing about the weather in Chicago is that it’s always changing.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.440
It can be very hot or very cold.

00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:22.144
In the summer, it’s mostly sunny and sometimes cloudy,

00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.300
with temperatures of about 84 degrees.

00:00:26.621 --> 00:00:29.085
And of course, sometimes it rains.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:36.372
In the winter, the temperature is usually between 29 and 14 degrees.

00:00:36.645 --> 00:00:42.810
It can be below freezing (32 degrees) for weeks at a time. Brrr!

00:00:44.071 --> 00:00:47.279
It snows about 38 inches a year.

00:00:49.032 --> 00:00:53.160
In the spring and the fall, the weather is very changeable –

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.856
you can have all four seasons in one week!

00:00:59.296 --> 00:01:01.906
It can be cold and snowing on Monday,

00:01:03.319 --> 00:01:09.204
cool and foggy on Tuesday, and warm and sunny on Wednesday.

00:01:10.341 --> 00:01:17.281
It’s a good idea for tourists to bring a winter coat, gloves, sunglasses, sandals,

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:22.138
and an umbrella when they visit Chicago in the spring and the fall –

00:01:22.726 --> 00:01:26.083
that way they are prepared for any kind of weather!

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:32.562
But one thing that isn’t always true about Chicago is the wind.

00:01:33.188 --> 00:01:38.851
Even though Chicago’s nickname is “The Windy City,” it’s not always windy there.

00:01:39.657 --> 00:01:43.676
In fact, Boston has more windy days than Chicago.

00:01:44.669 --> 00:01:50.440
Some people think Chicago’s nickname is from politicians who talk too much!